\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overall view of the pipeline. The URDF file is the sole structural input: it feeds RNEA, which produces the analytical term $\ensuremath  {\tau _{\mathrm  {rbd}}}$, never learned (grey background). Only GreyBoxNet and FrictionNet (thick outlines) are trained. The three loss terms are made explicit, together with the gradient flows (dashed) that connect them to the networks: $\mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {data}}$ fits the prediction, $\mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {torque}}$ and $\mathcal  {L}_{\mathrm  {dissip}}$ penalise violations of \cref  {eq-probleme}. Dissipativity constrains FrictionNet specifically, whose structure~\eqref  {eq-Dmat} moreover guarantees it by construction.}}{8}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig-pipeline}{{1}{8}{Overall view of the pipeline. The URDF file is the sole structural input: it feeds RNEA, which produces the analytical term $\taurbd $, never learned (grey background). Only GreyBoxNet and FrictionNet (thick outlines) are trained. The three loss terms are made explicit, together with the gradient flows (dashed) that connect them to the networks: $\mathcal {L}_{\mathrm {data}}$ fits the prediction, $\mathcal {L}_{\mathrm {torque}}$ and $\mathcal {L}_{\mathrm {dissip}}$ penalise violations of \cref {eq-probleme}. Dissipativity constrains FrictionNet specifically, whose structure~\eqref {eq-Dmat} moreover guarantees it by construction}{figure.caption.15}{}}
\newlabel{fig-pipeline@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][7][]8}}
